{
 "about": "Default fixed cameras for a 0.8 m T-pose character facing -Y (metres, Z up). `view`/`centre`/`size` give the orthographic shot used by kit2_view; `position`/`target`/`fov` (vertical degrees, camera 2.5 m from the target, square frame) give the same framing as a perspective camera for the live watch. below = camera below and in front, looking up at the waist. foot-*-side, foot-*-34 and elbow-* were added after the foot and elbow faults of the first character run lay outside every fixed view; the elbow cameras look at the rim of the cuff from in front and from inboard. feet-top and foot-*-side/-34 are placed from the character's own measurements by scripts/steps/kit2_cams.py at capture/render time; the numbers here are the fallback for a 0.8 m T-pose character. arm-left-end / arm-right-end are placed per character from the reference's measured arm (fingertip, wrist, elbow) by kit2_cams.py; the numbers here are the fallback for the 0.8 m character.",
